<Step id="STEP_5_VERIFY">
      <Goal>Let the CLI run and attest one complete mechanical phase-verification attempt.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run verification ToolCall below
        (`AX_PERMITTED_BASH_COMMANDS`, `AX_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_HANDOFF`). This is the one mechanical owner: it derives profile, exact
        Target Files, owning spec and applicable §Verification rows from the ticket; performs exact-target
        repair under a runtime before/after write-zone (any outside mutation is listed, left intact and
        halts before foundation; `.git` metadata and installed `node_modules` are excluded tool-state), one foundation run, then those read-only extra rows sequentially under
        a zero-write boundary; and only on complete success
        atomically records the structured phase receipt in Execution Log. Do not reconstruct arguments,
        run a §5 row yourself, add `ver` attestations, or duplicate the command within one attempt. Required coverage keeps
        one producer followed by its read/check row; not-applicable invents neither. `setup` may honestly
        skip absent bootstrap bricks; code/test fail closed. The receipt is mechanical evidence, not the
        semantic Handoff in STEP_6.

        On failure, fix only inside this phase's Target Files (regardless of age), then start a new attempt
        with the same command. Restore/remove a tombstone only through its declared `Deleted Files` outcome;
        tombstones are never repair targets. If remediation belongs to specs, another phase, or shared config this phase did not create,
        write strict JSON `{ "reason": "...", "axiom": "AX_...", "unblock": "..." }` to
        `.claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-blocker.json`, run blockerLog ToolCall below, and halt
        `H_BLOCKED`; never widen the write zone. An
        out-of-inventory export is removed or logged as `intro <name> ← <reason>` for audit backflow
        (`AX_CLOSED_WORLD_INVENTORY`); failure pauses or fails by `AX_HALT_VS_FAIL_DISTINCTION`;
        unsafe casts are removed or explicitly justified per `AX_NO_SILENT_ESCAPE_HATCH`.
        If the same in-zone verification failure remains after its fixes, or its required tooling is
        unavailable, halt `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL`; a checked phase without a receipt is never an exit.
        Once the cause is actually gone, write exact remediation to the phase log payload and run
        resolutionLog ToolCall below into THIS SAME phase block, per `AX_BLOCKER_RESOLUTION_TRAIL`;
        logged by whoever resumes the ticket (this phase's own retry, or the orchestrator), never a manual `Edit`.
        Inputs <ticket>: STEP_1 ticket identity.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="verification">npx gennady sdd-verify --task <ticket-path> --phase <PhaseID></ToolCall> Inputs <ticket-path>: <ticket-path>=canonical path returned by STEP_1; <PhaseID>=exact STEP_1 phase. Use verification.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="blockerLog">npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> blocker --payload-file .claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-blocker.json --phase <PhaseID></ToolCall> Use blockerLog.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="resolutionLog">npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> resolved --content-file .claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-log.txt --phase <PhaseID></ToolCall> Use resolutionLog.
      </Action>
    </Step>

<Axiom id="AX_CLOSED_WORLD_INVENTORY">
      Entity inventory is a closed world. For every module the agent lists ALL entities explicitly. Phrases like «и т.д.», «etc.», «and similar» are forbidden. Before approval, the agent makes the explicit drift-commitment captured in `ENTITY_INVENTORY_FORMAT`.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_NO_SILENT_ESCAPE_HATCH">
      A type-system escape hatch — a cast (`as any` / `as unknown` / `as never`, type assertions) or a suppression (`@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`) — defeats the static guarantees the code relies on. Default: do not use one — model the type properly (narrowing, guards, generics, discriminated unions). When one is genuinely unavoidable it is surfaced and justified in writing, never silent: a documented `@ts-expect-error <reason>` carrying a Decision Log reference (`<ACR>-DL-N`) that states why it is needed and why the alternatives do not work. A bare cast hides the problem; a documented suppression names it. Enforced mechanically by `CastSafetyCheck` and `DisablesCheck`.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_HANDOFF">
      Phase cannot emit Handoff without one successful `sdd-verify --task <ticket-path> --phase <PhaseID>`. The CLI, not the phase agent, structurally selects and runs the ladder plus every applicable ticket §5 command verbatim, then atomically writes their exact command/role/exit evidence and Target File state as the phase receipt. Any failure writes no reusable receipt and keeps the phase `[~] IN_PROGRESS` until resolved or escalated.

      **MANDATORY (PROTOCOL) — Canonical Gate Rule:** Ticket §5 commands are CANONICAL and CANNOT be substituted. Diagnostics may run while fixing, but only the canonical phase command can create completion evidence; a hand-written `ver` line is not evidence.

      The canon covers the script's BODY, not just its name in §5. Editing what a §5 script actually runs
      (e.g. rewriting `"typecheck"` in `package.json` so it does less, or points elsewhere) while logging the
      unchanged §5 command name is the same violation — the command stayed canonical on paper while its
      behavior was substituted underneath it. The one exception: `package.json`
      (or the script body) is itself among this phase's Target Files AND the change to that script IS the
      phase's stated Objective (a `bootstrap` / `config` phase whose job is exactly to define or rewire the
      script) — then the edit is legitimate work, not a gate dodge, and MUST be recorded as its own decision
      line in the Execution Log (`<ts> decision <script> rewritten ← <reason>`) before the gate runs.

      `sdd-verify --task <ticket-path> --phase <PhaseID>` is NOT supplemental — it owns STEP_5, including §5 extras (see `AX_PERMITTED_BASH_COMMANDS`). §5 therefore holds only EXTRA commands beyond the standard ladder and never repeats `sdd-verify`.

      Phase kind `doc` typically has no verification — empty section is acceptable.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_PERMITTED_BASH_COMMANDS">
      This role's bash commands stay within this list:
      - **Must run:** exact `sdd-verify --task <ticket-path> --phase <PhaseID>` exactly once per attempt at the phase
        protocol's STEP_5. That step owns repair order, target derivation and foundation semantics;
        this axiom only permits the invocation. Never wrap it in whole-project `npm run fix`, and
        never run the audit-owned `sdd-verify --profile full` from a phase. Its receipt is the result;
        do not copy it into prose log lines.
      - **May run:** `ls <dir>` for targeted recon (NOT `-la` or recursive); `tsc --noEmit` after code changes; `node --test <specific test file>` for test-kind phases; `date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ` for timestamps.
      - **May run:** `sdd-extract <file> <NAME>` — extract anchored section from ticket/spec.
      - **May run:** exact `unlink <declared Deleted File>` and `rmdir <declared Deleted File directory>` while implementing the phase; no glob, recursion, or undeclared deletion. A failed verification has no receipt, so a retry after the fix is a new attempt and invokes the canonical command once again.
      - **May run:** `gennady lint --spec=<module-spec> <paths>` only for a genuinely additional explicit check outside phase verification. STEP_5 already passes the owning spec and exact phase targets internally; do not duplicate it there.
      - **Bootstrap-only dependency addition:** ONLY when phase kind is `bootstrap`, its Objective names
        adding that dependency, and Target Files contain `package.json` plus the active npm lock file,
        may run exactly `npm view <pkg> engines`, `npm view <pkg> version`, and `npm view <pkg> dist-tags`,
        then one-package `npm install --save-dev --save-exact <pkg>@<verified-stable-version>` or
        `npm add --save-dev --save-exact <pkg>@<verified-stable-version>` for a dev tool; for a runtime
        dependency, one-package `npm install <pkg>@<verified-stable-version>` or
        `npm add <pkg>@<verified-stable-version>`. No other npm/network command, option, tag, unversioned
        package, or multi-package install is permitted. Non-bootstrap phases have no dependency-addition
        exemption.

      Trust the context handed at dispatch — ticket, spec, manifest, diff — as current: it MUST be
      used as-is, not re-derived through bash. When a step in this directive names a real gap beyond
      what was handed (new commits since dispatch, a sibling branch, a file's history), `git`/`gh`
      reads (`status`, `log`, `diff`, `show`, `blame`, `gh pr view`/`diff`) are the legal way to close
      it. Mutating the repository (`git add`/`commit`/`push`/`rebase`/`reset`, `gh pr create`/`merge`)
      stays reserved for the step that owns publish/commit.

      Absent such a step, treat `git`/`gh` as off the table: re-deriving handed context costs
      ~100-300ms per call for zero value, and full project recon / repository mutation belong to the
      orchestrator or authoring flow, not this role.

      All recon stays inside the project root. A fact that genuinely lives outside it — a global
      `~/.npmrc`, a system-wide setting, anything outside this checkout — is not a gap this role closes
      by reading it anyway, read-only or not: no bash command in this list reaches outside the project
      root, and none should be improvised to. That fact is `H_BLOCKED` per `AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION` with
      the specific question named — the operator is the channel for what the sandbox cannot see, not a
      last resort after trying anyway.

      **Temp files stay under `.claude/tmp/`, nowhere else.** Any scratch or trial file this role
      needs — a throwaway script, an intermediate probe output — is created ONLY under `.claude/tmp/`
      inside the project root: create the directory when it does not yet exist, and remove what was
      created once it stops being needed (shared, reused across roles and other purposes — not
      this phase's private space to leave dirty). The system `/tmp`, `$TMPDIR`, and the repository
      root are closed for this: a root-level scratch file pollutes the diff and gets caught by the
      same inventory/lint gates meant for real `Target Files`, and `/tmp`/`$TMPDIR` sit outside the
      checkout this role's recon is scoped to above.

      **Forbidden:** any npm/network command outside the exact bootstrap-only forms above; `npm run fix`; `npm run check`; `npm run lint` alone (overkill — use `sdd-verify` or `tsc --noEmit` for narrower checks); `npm run format`; `prettier` directly — repair and verification both live INSIDE `sdd-verify`, never called piecemeal; any recursive or project-wide file scan; any command that reads unrelated files for «context».

      Ticket §5 commands are not a phase-agent exemption: the one `sdd-verify --task ... --phase ...`
      invocation runs applicable rows itself and owns their receipt (`AX_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_HANDOFF`).
      `sdd-verify` remains the sole self-initiated mutator through its exact-target repair rung; a
      standalone §5, format, lint or fix invocation remains forbidden.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_HALT_VS_FAIL_DISTINCTION">
      Halt is NOT failure. A skill or phase that stops awaiting operator decision is in a **PAUSED** state, not a **FAILED** state. Surface to operator with distinct semantics:

      - **✋ PAUSED — awaiting operator decision**: orchestrator detected unresolved BLOCKER per `AX_BLOCKER_RESOLUTION_TRAIL`, or phase agent returned `BLOCKED` per `AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION`, or planning surface revealed `[!] BLOCKED` in Phases Overview. Skill is fully functional; it is waiting for a decision or environmental fix. To resume: operator addresses the blocker, then re-runs the skill.
      - **❌ FAILED — skill malfunction**: skill cannot proceed due to missing rule files, malformed ticket structure beyond scaffold convention, infrastructure unreachable, or other reasons unrelated to operator decisions. To resume: fix the infrastructure issue.
      - **⚠️ AUDIT FAIL — verification mismatch**: phases completed but audit found discrepancies. Has its own retry path (per `phase_audit_loop`).

      Operator-facing messages MUST use the icon and word for the actual state. Misusing `❌` for a paused state is itself a self-deception that erodes trust in skill output (treated as fabricated halt; orchestrator must correct).
    </Axiom>